    {
      "text": "brought before governors and kings, Matt. 10:18 (Mark 13:9; Luke 21:12). they that wear soft clothing are in kings’ houses, Matt. 11:8. of whom do the kings of the earth take custom, Matt. 17:25. like unto a certain king, which made a marriage, Matt. 22:2. ye shall be brought before rulers and kings, Mark 13:9. prophets and kings have desired to see those things, Luke 10:24. kings of the Gentiles exercise lordship over them, Luke 22:25. We have no king but Cæsar, John 19:15. bear my name before the Gentiles, and kings, Acts 9:15. For kings, and for all that are in authority, 1 Tim. 2:2. Fear God. Honour the king, 1 Pet. 2:17. kings of the earth, and the great men, Rev. 6:15. way of the kings of the east might be prepared, Rev. 16:12. there are seven kings, Rev. 17:10. ten horns which thou sawest are ten kings, Rev. 17:12. kings of the earth do bring their glory, Rev. 21:24.",
